1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,432
To anyone far away,

2
00:00:01,432 --> 00:00:02,971
you'd freeze at the
edge.

3
00:00:03,321 --> 00:00:05,985
Friends far away would
watch you slow down.

4
00:00:05,985 --> 00:00:07,838
Then stop, just short of
the edge.

5
00:00:08,338 --> 00:00:10,328
That edge is the event
horizon.

6
00:00:10,328 --> 00:00:11,835
Point of no return.

7
00:00:11,835 --> 00:00:13,304
Not even light escapes.

8
00:00:13,704 --> 00:00:14,506
Why?

9
00:00:14,506 --> 00:00:17,109
Gravity bends space and
time so hard,

10
00:00:17,109 --> 00:00:19,095
your picture slows to a
stop.

11
00:00:19,745 --> 00:00:22,476
On your own clock,
NASA's simulation says,

12
00:00:22,476 --> 00:00:24,571
the fall takes about
three hours.

13
00:00:25,021 --> 00:00:28,289
A giant black hole,
about four million Suns.

14
00:00:28,289 --> 00:00:30,417
Like the one in our
galaxy's center.

15
00:00:30,917 --> 00:00:31,958
Cross the edge,

16
00:00:31,958 --> 00:00:34,951
and space itself rushes
inward at light speed.

17
00:00:35,251 --> 00:00:37,060
Then the simulation
gives you

18
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:38,748
twelve point eight
seconds,

19
00:00:38,748 --> 00:00:40,255
before you're torn
apart.

20
00:00:40,405 --> 00:00:42,816
The closer end of you
gets pulled harder.

21
00:00:42,816 --> 00:00:44,208
You stretch like a
noodle.

22
00:00:44,358 --> 00:00:46,855
Scientists really call
it spaghettification.

23
00:00:47,455 --> 00:00:49,335
A small black hole is
worse.

24
00:00:49,335 --> 00:00:51,484
It can tear you apart
before the edge.

25
00:00:51,984 --> 00:00:52,913
At the center,

26
00:00:52,913 --> 00:00:55,220
math says a point of
endless crush.

27
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:56,882
Nobody knows if it's
real.

28
00:00:57,582 --> 00:00:59,759
Nothing from inside can
reach us.

29
00:00:59,759 --> 00:01:01,371
This is math, not a
memory.

30
00:01:02,071 --> 00:01:03,139
The verdict?

31
00:01:03,139 --> 00:01:04,008
Unproven.

32
00:01:05,308 --> 00:01:06,540
To anyone far away,

33
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:08,219
you'd freeze at the
edge.

34
00:01:08,219 --> 00:01:09,960
To you, you'd fall right
through.

